    "q-335025": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335025",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*",
      "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-335025-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]",
